      "summary": "Add custom theme support (#1472)",
      "description": "* themes: add custom theme support (export, load, auto-discovery)\n\nAdd CustomBundlePath + FormatVersion to ThemePreset for bundle-based\nloading. Extend ThemeContainer to track and unload AssetBundles.\n\nMake ThemeComponent getters null-safe — missing fields return empty\ncollections instead of throwing, enabling forward-compatible fallback\nto default theme for incomplete/old custom themes.\n\nAdd editor export tool ([ContextMenu] + custom inspector) that packages\ntheme prefab + Metal shader sub-bundle into .yargtheme ZIP archive.\n\nOverride ThemePresetContainer.Initialize() to scan custom/themes/ for\n.yargtheme files, extract ZIPs, deserialize metadata, and register\ndiscovered themes. Themes appear in existing profile dropdown automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: pi-coding-agent <pi-coding-agent>\nModel: Qwen3.6-27B\n\n* themes: switch from ZIP to single AssetBundle\n\n.yargtheme is now a raw AssetBundle with metadata embedded as a\nTextAsset (\"theme_meta\") instead of a ZIP containing separate JSON\nand bundle files.\n\nExport: serialize ThemePreset to TextAsset, include with prefab\n(\"ThemeRoot\") in single bundle build. No ZIP creation, no temp\ndirectories.\n\nLoad: AssetBundle.LoadFromFile(), read theme_meta TextAsset,\ndeserialize preset. Zero extraction, no stale dirs in custom/themes/.\n\nAlso: single CollectDependencies pass (was two), bundle output named\nafter theme file for uniqueness, prefab name \"ThemeRoot\" avoids\ncase-sensitivity issues with \"_theme.prefab\" on Linux.\n\nCo-Authored-By: pi-coding-agent <pi-coding-agent>\nModel: Qwen3.6-27B\n\n* Refactor to share bundle export/loading code between characters/venues/themes\n\n* fix(themes): skip JSON loading for theme presets\n\nThemes are loaded from .yargtheme bundles, not JSON files. Calling\nbase.Initialize() loaded nonexistent JSON presets that lacked\nCustomBundlePath, causing NotImplementedException in\nCreateThemeContainer().\n\nJust create the directory and scan for *.yargtheme files directly.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: pi-coding-agent <pi-coding-agent>"
